{
  "_doc": [
    "The thing people picture when they picture the place.",
    "",
    "Everything automatic we tried produced photos that were technically correct",
    "and commercially useless. Text search matched the word, not the place",
    "(a moth for Rome). Geosearch fixed the location and gave us photos that were",
    "genuinely shot in the city and still worthless: a bus stop for Houston, a",
    "police car for Grand Cayman, a bike rack for Nashville. Nothing in a",
    "coordinate or a licence tells you which view of a city makes someone want to",
    "go there.",
    "",
    "So that judgement is written down instead of inferred. Each city lists the",
    "views worth showing, best first, and the fetcher tries them in order. Curated",
    "is the honest answer here: it is 32 cities, they change on the timescale of",
    "decades, and a human naming Pike Place Market beats any ranking function we",
    "could write.",
    "",
    "Adding a city: add its code with 3-6 entries, most iconic first. Prefer views",
    "with scale (skylines, coastlines, plazas) over interiors and close-ups, and",
    "name the landmark the way Commons would title it."
  ],
